[2025-04-29 20:23:31] PROPOSAL by EU:
Title: **Title:**
Global Climate Action Compact: Equitable Carbon Tax Framework

**Proposal:**  
In recognition of the urgent threat of climate change and the necessity of collective action, this committee proposes the establishment of a Global Carbon Tax Framework rooted in the principles of equity, shared responsibility, and economic resilience.

**Action Items:**

1. **Implementation of a Graduated Global Carbon Tax:**  
A globally binding carbon tax, initially set at an agreed baseline, will be levied on fossil fuel emissions. Tax rates will be differentiated based on countries’ historical emissions, current economic capacity, and development status, ensuring higher rates for developed nations and a phased approach for developing economies. Least-developed countries will receive temporary exemptions or significantly reduced rates.

2. **Climate Finance and Technology Transfer Fund:**  
All revenues generated from the carbon tax will contribute to an international fund managed transparently by a multilateral agency. This fund will support climate mitigation and adaptation in developing and highly vulnerable countries, and facilitate global access to green technologies, ensuring no nation is left behind in the energy transition.

3. **Robust Monitoring and Just Transition Mechanisms:**  
Establish an independent international body to monitor, report, and verify emissions and revenue use. The framework will include provisions for regular review to adjust tax rates and exemptions. Mechanisms for supporting a “just transition” for workers and communities most affected by decarbonization will also be integrated.

**Conclusion:**  
This proposal balances ambition with fairness, addressing climate imperatives while respecting national circumstances. It invites all member states to commit to binding, transparent global action, with flexibility and equity at its core. We urge broad support and timely adoption.

