This proposal, rooted in fairness and sustainable development, is cognizant of various national conditions and capacities. It holds developed nations accountable for their historical responsibilities, while providing mechanisms for developing nations to grow in a sustainable manner. Balancing ecological wellbeing with economic progress, this proposal aligns with the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) and the Paris Agreement, delivering a politically viable solution to one of the most pressing issues of our time.



